WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.425
Build an evaluation set from real workflows using approved representative data.

00:00:04.425 --> 00:00:08.875
Include common tasks, difficult cases, ambiguous requests, stale sources,

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.760
permission boundaries, and costly errors.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.260
Define expected outcomes before reviewing results.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.150
Measure answer quality, citation support, hallucinations, refusal behavior,

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.610
structured output, latency, prompt processing, generation speed, memory, temperature,

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.900
failure rate, and recovery.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.360
Repeat important tests because model output can vary.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:26.860
Test the complete application.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:32.065
Retrieval, document parsing, prompts, tools, API limits, authentication, interface state,

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:34.930
and logs can fail even when the base model performs well.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.660
Track where the failure occurred.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.160
Collect user feedback tied to tasks rather than general enthusiasm.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.500
Did the assistant save time, improve quality, or create review work?

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.170
Preserve examples of false confidence, missing sources, poor formatting,

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.225
and unsafe actions.

00:00:48.225 --> 00:00:53.120
Model, runtime, driver, document, prompt, and configuration updates need versioning,

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.590
regression tests, change approval, backups, and rollback.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.080
Rebuilding an index can change answers even when the model stays the same.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:03.160
Monitor availability, queues, resource use, unauthorized access, data growth,

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.580
stale content, errors, and quality trends.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.905
Expand users, sources,

00:01:06.905 --> 00:01:11.010
or automation only when existing workflows are reliable and operational ownership is

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:11.450
clear.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:16.300
Define service objectives for uptime, latency, quality, support response, backup recovery,

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.320
and index freshness.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:22.545
Objectives make tradeoffs visible and show when the assistant needs capacity, redesign,

00:01:22.545 --> 00:01:22.960
or retirement.
